# The default Flatpaks. Installed system-wide from the flathub remote, once:
# by pulsar-flatpaks.service on the first boot that has a network, or by
# `sudo pulsar setup apps` if you would rather watch it happen. After that
# first success the service never runs again, so removing an app on a
# running system sticks -- this list is a starting set, not enforced state.
#
# One application ID per line; '#' starts a comment. Curation rules: the
# launchers and daily drivers a fresh install is actually missing, nothing
# Microsoft-owned, nothing an average boot does not use.

# launchers -- the out-of-box gap between a fresh image and a playable one
com.valvesoftware.Steam
io.github.Faugus.faugus-launcher

# plumbing -- proton management, sandbox permissions, wine prefixes
com.vysp3r.ProtonPlus
com.github.tchx84.Flatseal
com.usebottles.bottles

# daily drivers
com.discordapp.Discord
com.obsproject.Studio
com.github.wwmm.easyeffects
